{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBTVJEFUg4Whdiv6dsNJ2d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Problem\n2\t\n3\t`attavo doctor` reported done on this repository on 2026-09-17 while none of its three traversals (#106, #148, #153) had a statement in the attestation store: `main` had classic protection and no merge queue, every merge was direct, the coherence workflow's `merge_group` trigger never fired, and proof two holds on the four stage records with the chain held without asking whether the merge was sealed. The store answers 404 for all three; the operator screen rendered the missing statements as `not read`.\n4\t\n5\tRetires: the doctor's `done` on an unattested traversal; `not read` as the rendering of a statement that does not exist.\n6\t\n7\t## Claims\n8\t\n9\t- bin/attavo\n10\t- schema/manifest.schema.json\n11\t- attavo.toml\n12\t- .attavo/bin/forge-attestation\n13\t- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n14\t- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\n15\t- tests/test_doctor.py\n16\t\n17\t## Criteria\n18\t\n19\t- doctor-fails-on-an-unsealed-merge.sh: on a fixture tenant with two merged items whose [forge].attestation_command answers for one merge and not the other, attavo doctor --json fails proof every-attested-item-is-sealed naming item 2 and its merge sha, listing sealed and unsealed, and holds once the command answers for both\n20\t- doctor-fails-without-attestation-command.sh: a manifest with no [forge].attestation_command fails the proof naming the key, and the manifest schema declares the key\n21\t- the-proof-has-its-test.sh: a test named test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge exists under tests/, this repository's manifest names its attestation command, and .attavo/bin/forge-attestation is executable\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a170d87-3d29-46e3-a1eb-69574ae98490","uuid":"b597f155-6920-49e4-8849-81e64d4b97cd","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:39:22.736Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-158/attest/specs/158/spec.md","content":"## Problem\n\n`attavo doctor` reported done on this repository on 2026-09-17 while none of its three traversals (#106, #148, #153) had a statement in the attestation store: `main` had classic protection and no merge queue, every merge was direct, the coherence workflow's `merge_group` trigger never fired, and proof two holds on the four stage records with the chain held without asking whether the merge was sealed. The store answers 404 for all three; the operator screen rendered the missing statements as `not read`.\n\nRetires: the doctor's `done` on an unattested traversal; `not read` as the rendering of a statement that does not exist.\n\n## Claims\n\n- bin/attavo\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- attavo.toml\n- .attavo/bin/forge-attestation\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml\n- tests/test_doctor_sealed.py\n- tests/test_doctor.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- doctor-fails-on-an-unsealed-merge.sh: on a fixture tenant with two merged items whose [forge].attestation_command answers for one merge and not the other, attavo doctor --json fails proof every-attested-item-is-sealed naming item 2 and its merge sha, listing sealed and unsealed, and holds once the command answers for both\n- doctor-fails-without-attestation-command.sh: a manifest with no [forge].attestation_command fails the proof naming the key, and the manifest schema declares the key\n- the-proof-has-its-test.sh: a test named test_doctor_proof_six_fails_on_an_unsealed_merge exists under tests/, this repository's manifest names its attestation command, and .attavo/bin/forge-attestation is executable\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
